  "walkthroughs": [
    {
      "tag": "Letters",
      "h2": "Italian Volume",
      "body_html": "<p>Italian terms label dynamics. From quietest to loudest: <strong>pp</strong> (pianissimo), <strong>p</strong> (piano), <strong>mp</strong>, <strong>mf</strong>, <strong>f</strong> (forte), <strong>ff</strong> (fortissimo).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Change",
      "h2": "Crescendo & Diminuendo",
      "body_html": "<p>To get gradually <strong>louder</strong>, write <strong>crescendo</strong> (or a < hairpin). To get gradually <strong>quieter</strong>, write <strong>diminuendo</strong> (or > hairpin).</p>"
    },
    {
      "tag": "Use",
      "h2": "Why Dynamics Matter",
      "body_html": "<p>A piece all at the same volume becomes boring. Dramatic dynamics — a sudden <strong>ff</strong> after <strong>pp</strong> — make the listener jump. Music breathes through dynamics.</p>"
    }
  ],
